@startuml Build Failure Scenarios

title Build Failure — Timeout Detection & Race Condition Handling

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F4F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #DAA520
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFACD
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness 1
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #999999
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

actor       "User"               as U
participant "Web Frontend"       as FE
participant "Backend API"        as BE
participant "Automation Worker"  as W
participant "Proxmox Hypervisor" as PX

== Normal Start (Abbreviated) ==

note over U, PX
  Normal flow: worker claims job, VM provisioned, scripts executing.
end note

W -> BE : PATCH …/progress (stage=EXECUTE_SCRIPTS, percent=33)
BE --> W : 200 ACK

== Worker Failure ==

note over W #FFCCCC
  WORKER CRASH
  Process terminates, VM hangs,
  or network partition occurs.
  Worker does NOT deregister.
end note

...

== Timeout Detection ==

note over BE
  ScheduledTasksService fires every 60s.
  markStaleJobsAsFailed checks lastProgressAt
  (no-progress silence), NOT the heartbeat:
  10 min in BUILDING, 35 min in EXPORTING.
  The /ping liveness call updates only
  workerLastHeartbeatAt, so a hung script still
  ages out lastProgressAt and fails.
  Hard cap: markLongRunningJobsAsFailed at
  3-hour wall-clock, regardless of progress.
end note

BE -> BE : markStaleJobsAsFailed()\nstate: BUILDING → FAILED

== Frontend Discovers Failure ==

FE -> BE : GET /api/builds/{id}
BE --> FE : {state=FAILED, failureReason}
FE --> U  : Display failure reason

== Race Condition: Slow Worker Completes After Timeout ==

note over W #FEF5E7
  Worker was slow, not crashed.
  Build finished after backend already
  marked the job FAILED.
end note

W -[#FF6600]-> BE : POST …/complete\n(late attempt)

BE -> BE : canTransitionTo(FAILED → READY)?\nResult: FALSE

BE -[#CC0000]-> W : 409 Conflict

note over W #FFE5E5
  Worker catches 409 after 3 retry attempts.
  The exception propagates to run()'s handler:
  _cleanup_vm() deletes the Proxmox build VM and
  _cleanup_export_artifacts() removes the OVA from
  the worker export path (NFR7). fail_job() is then
  called. (Only an SFTP transfer interrupted mid-copy
  leaves an orphaned partial OVA for the cron sweep.)
end note

note over BE #E8DAEF
  State machine prevents double-registration.
  A FAILED job cannot transition to READY
  regardless of what the worker sends.
end note

@enduml
